data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Tested with .NET 11 (preview) and it works without issues:

```csharp
Span<nint> nints = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

Both `nint` (signed) and `nuint` (unsigned) native-sized integers work as expected. On this 64-bit system they behave as 8-byte integers (`nint.MaxValue` = `long.MaxValue`). This feature has been available since C# 9 / .NET 5, when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced.
